9. Foundry equation and search object

Let:

• (O) be an operator;
• (D) a destination domain;
• (B) a basis;
• (E) an environment;
• (\phi_{D,E}) an encoder;
• (\psi_{D,E}) a decoder;
• (\mathcal{H}) a harvester of invariants, mutations, jams, and residuals.

Then a Foundry trial is

[ Y(O,D,B,E;x)

\mathcal{H}\left(
\psi_{D,E}\left[B^{-1}OB\left(\phi_{D,E}(x)\right)\right],
\delta
\right).
]

The expression is architectural, not a claim that every operator or basis is linear. Its invariant is the sequence:

```text
encode → choose coordinates → operate → restore coordinates → decode
→ compare with reality → harvest result and delta
```

